<name>CVT System [Super CVT-i] (K112/K112F)</name>
<para id="RM000000FU100OX" category="C" type-id="303M0" name-id="3225W-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>P0962/62</dtccode>
<dtcname>DS1 Solenoid Circuit (Low)</dtcname>
<dtccode>P0963/62</dtccode>
<dtcname>DS1 Solenoid Circuit (High)</dtcname>
<dtccode>P0966/63</dtccode>
<dtcname>DS2 Solenoid Circuit (Low)</dtcname>
<dtccode>P0967/63</dtccode>
<dtcname>DS2 Solenoid Circuit (High)</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000000FU100OX_01" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000046U00000">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The engine control computer controls the inflow and outflow of line pressure to and from the primary pulley according to vehicle speed and accelerator opening, using signals to solenoid DS1 (for inflow to the primary pulley) and solenoid DS2 (for outflow from the primary pulley). As a fail-safe function, if a solenoid is short-circuited or open, the engine control computer stops energizing the malfunctioning solenoid.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="0.93in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.97in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="3.18in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Condition</ptxt>
<ptxt>1. Detection condition 2. Malfunction status 3. Malfunction duration 4. Other</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Inspection Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
