<subpara id="RM000000FU100OX_03" type-id="51" category="05">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000FU100OX_04" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM000000FU100OX_04_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___000046W00000">
<testtitle>Perform TaSCAN Active Test (Shift Position)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), following the screen instructions, display the [Active Test] screen and perform the Active Test.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<table pgwide="1">
<title>[Diagnosis screen: Powertrain → TCCS → Active Test]</title>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.47in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.63in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.99in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Item Name</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Test Details</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Restrictions</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Shift Position</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Can be set to any shift position (reference gear ratio)</ptxt>
<ptxt>[1(2.4)/2(1.5)/3(1.0)/4(0.7)/5(0.43)]</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Test is canceled when vehicle speed is less than 20km/h or 45km/h or more</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.07in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.06in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>NG</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>OK</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000FU100OX_04_0002" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="RM000000FU100OX_04_0013" fin="false">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000FU100OX_04_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___000046X00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Continuously Variable Transaxle Assembly (Solenoid [DS1/DS2])</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the transmission wire connector.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C102330J42" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the terminals of the connector.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.71in"/>
<colspec colname="COLSPEC0" colwidth="1.17in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.25in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Name)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>5 (DS1) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>11 to 13Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10 (DS2) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>11 to 13Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000FU100OX_04_0003" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000000FU100OX_04_0014" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000FU100OX_04_0003" proc-id="RM0550J___000046Y00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness and Connector (Continuously Variable Transaxle [Transmission Wire] - Engine Control Computer)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the wire harness and connector inspection procedure and precautions, see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000005D701ZX"/>.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect the transmission wire connector.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C159285J04" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect engine control computer connector A, and using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between each terminal. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM000000FSD00RX"/> for Terminals of ECU)</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.39in"/>
<colspec colname="COLSPEC3" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COLSPEC2" colwidth="1.36in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Name)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A79(DS1) - A104(E1)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>11 to 13Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A78(DS2) - A104(E1)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>11 to 13Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000FU100OX_04_0013" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000000FU100OX_04_0011" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000FU100OX_04_0013">
<testtitle>Replace Engine Control Computer</testtitle>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000FU100OX_04_0006" fin="false">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000FU100OX_04_0006" proc-id="RM0550J___000046Z00000">
<scantool type="1"/>
<testtitle>TaSCAN (A/T / CVT Learned Value Initialization, G Sensor 0-point Learning and CVT Hydraulic Pressure Learning)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Initializing the learned values clears both the G sensor 0-point learning values and the CVT hydraulic pressure learning values, so when replacing the parts in the table below, perform AT/CVT learned value initialization and be sure to perform both G sensor 0-point learning and CVT hydraulic pressure learning.</ptxt>
<table>
<tgroup cols="1">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="4.13in"/>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry align="center">
<ptxt>Replacement Parts</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Continuously Variable Transaxle</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Engine Control Computer</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Skid control computer</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Oil Pressure Sensor</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Yaw Rate Sensor</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>After performing AT/CVT learned value initialization, be sure to perform G sensor 0-point learning first, and then CVT hydraulic pressure learning.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Be sure to place the vehicle on a level surface and perform 0 point learning.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Do not subject the vehicle to vibration while 0 point learning is in progress.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), perform A/T/CVT learned value initialization, G sensor 0 point learning and CVT hydraulic pressure learning.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the procedures for A/T/CVT learned value initialization, G sensor 0-point learning and CVT hydraulic pressure learning, refer to <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000021F400AX"/>.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check the DTCs again. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM000000FSM00TX"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000FU100OX_04_0012" fin="true">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000FU100OX_04_0014">
<testtitle>Replace Continuously Variable Transaxle Assembly</testtitle>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000FU100OX_04_0009" fin="false">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
